{"name":"Ginger Root","hex":"#c17444","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ginger root","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ginger, the underground stem, or rhizome, of the plant Zingiber officinale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ginger_root"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ginger Root (music project)","blocks":[{"text":"Ginger Root (姜根) is an American indie soul music project from Huntington Beach, California, led by singer-songwriter and instrumentalist Cameron Lew. Lew has described the project's musical sound as \"aggressive elevator soul\", also citing inspiration as coming from groups such as Vulfpeck, Toro y Moi, White Denim, Yellow Magic Orchestra, and Feist. On tour, Ginger Root has supported bands such as Khruangbin, Hippo Campus, Omar Apollo, Last Dinosaurs, and Japanese Breakfast as well as headlining their own tour in Fall of 2022, with supporting artists King Pari, Vicky Farewell, and Amaiwana."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Ginger_Root_in_Concert_2024.jpg/330px-Ginger_Root_in_Concert_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ginger_Root_(music_project)","wikidata":"Q104843780"},{"title":"Ginger","blocks":[{"text":"Ginger is a flowering plant whose rhizome, ginger root or ginger, is widely used as a spice and a folk medicine. It is an herbaceous perennial that grows annual pseudostems about one meter tall, bearing narrow leaf blades. The inflorescences bear flowers having pale yellow petals with purple edges, and arise directly from the rhizome on separate shoots."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Koeh-146-no_text.jpg/330px-Koeh-146-no_text.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ginger","wikidata":"Q35625"},{"title":"Root","blocks":[{"text":"In vascular plants, the roots are the organs of a plant that are modified to provide anchorage for the plant and take in water and nutrients into the plant body, which allows plants to grow taller and faster. They are most often below the surface of the soil, but roots can also be aerial or aerating, that is, growing up above the ground or especially above water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Primary_and_secondary_cotton_roots.jpg/330px-Primary_and_secondary_cotton_roots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Root","wikidata":"Q41500"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/GingerRoot_Novo_Los_Angeles.jpg/500px-GingerRoot_Novo_Los_Angeles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/GingerRoot_Novo_Los_Angeles.jpg/1280px-GingerRoot_Novo_Los_Angeles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/GingerRoot_Novo_Los_Angeles.jpg/500px-GingerRoot_Novo_Los_Angeles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ginger Root performing at the Novo in Los Angeles at the conclusion of their Nisemono Arc in 2023.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGingerRoot_Novo_Los_Angeles.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Ginger_Root_-_Cameron_Lew_%28Chinese_-%E5%88%98%E5%9B%BD%E6%98%8E%29_performing_at_Mahalls_Lakewood_Ohio_2024.jpg/500px-Ginger_Root_-_Cameron_Lew_%28Chinese_-%E5%88%98%E5%9B%BD%E6%98%8E%29_performing_at_Mahalls_Lakewood_Ohio_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Ginger_Root_-_Cameron_Lew_%28Chinese_-%E5%88%98%E5%9B%BD%E6%98%8E%29_performing_at_Mahalls_Lakewood_Ohio_2024.jpg/1280px-Ginger_Root_-_Cameron_Lew_%28Chinese_-%E5%88%98%E5%9B%BD%E6%98%8E%29_performing_at_Mahalls_Lakewood_Ohio_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Ginger_Root_-_Cameron_Lew_%28Chinese_-%E5%88%98%E5%9B%BD%E6%98%8E%29_performing_at_Mahalls_Lakewood_Ohio_2024.jpg/500px-Ginger_Root_-_Cameron_Lew_%28Chinese_-%E5%88%98%E5%9B%BD%E6%98%8E%29_performing_at_Mahalls_Lakewood_Ohio_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cameron Lew of Ginger Root performing at Mahall's in Lakewood, Ohio 2024.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGinger_Root_-_Cameron_Lew_(Chinese_-%E5%88%98%E5%9B%BD%E6%98%8E)_performing_at_Mahalls_Lakewood_Ohio_2024.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Ginger_inflorescence.jpg/500px-Ginger_inflorescence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Ginger_inflorescence.jpg/1280px-Ginger_inflorescence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Ginger_inflorescence.jpg/500px-Ginger_inflorescence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGinger_inflorescence.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Flower_of_Ginger1.jpg/500px-Flower_of_Ginger1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Flower_of_Ginger1.jpg/1280px-Flower_of_Ginger1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Flower_of_Ginger1.jpg/500px-Flower_of_Ginger1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ginger flower","